        },
        "body": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A bib gets washed two or three times a day. That's 700+ wash cycles in the first year alone. Most fabrics don't survive that — cotton stiffens, terry pills, and plastic-backed bibs start to smell. TENCEL™ Lyocell is built for exactly this.</p><p>It's a botanic fiber derived from eucalyptus wood pulp. Independent testing shows it absorbs moisture <strong>50% more efficiently than cotton</strong> — and unlike cotton, it releases that moisture quickly instead of holding it against your baby's skin. That means a bib that dries faster between meals and stays soft after hundreds of washes.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
