          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I wash a long sleeve bib?",
            "answer": "<p>Machine wash cold on a gentle cycle. Tumble dry low or hang dry. No bleach, no fabric softener — softener coats the fibres and reduces absorbency over time. For food stains, rinse or spot-treat before washing. TENCEL™ dries significantly faster than cotton, so a hang-dry is usually ready within a couple of hours.</p>"
          }
        },
        "size": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What size fits my baby?",
            "answer": "<p>The long sleeve bib is designed to fit babies from roughly 6 months through toddler age. The back snap closure is adjustable for a secure fit without being restrictive. Check the size guide on the product page for specific measurements.</p>"
          }
        },
        "stain": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I get food stains out?",
            "answer": "<p>Rinse immediately after use — most purees and soft foods come out easily in a cold wash. For tougher stains (berry, tomato, turmeric), apply a small amount of dish soap directly to the stain before washing. Avoid hot water — it can set protein-based stains.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
