    "faq": {
      "type": "collapsible-tabs",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does a long sleeve bib actually protect the outfit underneath?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — that's the entire point. The long sleeves cover the arms (where standard bibs fail completely) and the wide chest piece covers the front of the outfit. For most meals, a quick wipe-down of the bib is all you need. You're not doing a full outfit change every time your baby eats.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is TENCEL™ safe for contact with food?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. All Loulou Lollipop TENCEL™ products are OEKO-TEX® Standard 100 certified — independently tested and verified free from over 100 harmful substances, including heavy metals, pesticides, and harmful dyes. Safe for what goes near your baby's food and mouth.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How many long sleeve bibs do I need?",
            "answer": "<p>Most families find 3–4 works well. With TENCEL™ drying in 1–2 hours on a hang dry, you can turn bibs around quickly between meals. If you're doing laundry every other day, 3 is usually enough. 4–5 gives comfortable margin for messier phases like self-feeding with a spoon.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is it better than a plastic-backed bib?",
            "answer": "<p>Depends on what you're optimizing for. Plastic-backed bibs catch liquid but are uncomfortable against skin and don't dry flat — they hold moisture and can start to smell. TENCEL™ is breathable and comfortable for the full meal, washes completely clean, and doesn't develop odor the way plastic-backed options do. For a baby in the high chair 2–3 times a day, the comfort and wash performance of TENCEL™ makes it the better daily driver.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is TENCEL™ better than bamboo for bibs?",
            "answer": "<p>For something washed this frequently, yes. Bamboo rayon is soft initially but pills and thins faster through repeated washing. TENCEL™ Lyocell holds its surface and hand through hundreds of wash cycles. For a bib that sees 700+ washes in its first year, durability matters more than first-touch softness.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "At what age can my baby start using this bib?",
            "answer": "<p>From the start of solids — typically around 6 months. The adjustable back snap fits from early solids through toddler age. The long sleeves are equally useful for art, sensory play, and craft time as babies get older and messier in new and creative ways.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
